==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|persécuter|ang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|persequor||follow up, pursue|lang=la}}, from {{prefix|per|sequor|t1=through|t2=follow|lang=la}} (English {{term|sequel|lang=en}}). Compare {{term|prosecute|lang=en}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|persecut|ing}}

# To pursue in a manner to injure, grieve, or afflict; to beset with cruelty or malignity; to harass; especially, to afflict, harass, punish, or put to death for one's race, sexual identity, adherence to a particular religious creed, or mode of worship.
#: ''"Do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and '''persecute''' you."''  -Matt. v. 44.
# To harass with importunity; to pursue with persistent solicitations; to annoy.

